@Situation:	two EFL learners talk about how they celebrate holidays
@Comment:	Discourse codes on %cod as $CATEGORY:CODE. Utterance order is identical to data/holiday.cha; L numbers in README and holiday_coding.csv refer to that file.
@Comment:	NOM = negotiation of meaning (CR CC CMC); REP = repair (SSR OC); CST = communication strategy (WS APX CIRC APW CSW RES ABN MLC); INT = interaction (MIN ASM AGR DIS COL CMP); ORG = discourse organization (TSK TOP QI CLS)
@Comment:	Episodes are lazy gems (@G). E0 task opening; E1 MAR Christmas; E2 role switch; E3 MAR Chuseok; E4 LEX Chuseok rites; E5 Coco and Mexico; E6 food left vs eaten; E7 photo and spirits' food; E8 Peru cemetery and closing
